{"ts": "2026-08-17T12:43:46Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 74, "kind": "tool_use", "text": "Write", "meta": {"native_type": "assistant", "block_type": "tool_use", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01QyimjUA5iRn5gbW5YDVo3N", "input": {"file_path": "/home/dev/projects/test-project/docs/design.md", "content": "# Design: Give tasks a due date\n\n**Taiga:** #12\n**Spec:** `docs/spec.md`\n\n*Note: this overwrites `docs/design.md` from the previous cycle (Taiga #11),\nsame scratch-turnover reasoning as the spec.*\n\n## Conventions established\n\nReviewed `frontend/src/components/AddTask.jsx`, `TaskList.jsx`, `App.jsx`,\nand `frontend/src/App.css`. No component library \u2014 plain function\ncomponents, plain CSS, native HTML form controls (`<select>`, `<input>`).\nThe precedent this feature mirrors throughout is **priority**: a per-row\nnative control, styled with a `-select`/`-input` class plus a state\nmodifier class, changed directly from the row without an edit mode. Due\ndate follows the same shape, using `<input type=\"date\">` in place of\n`<select>`.\n\nOne useful fact confirmed directly, not assumed: Pydantic's default JSON\nencoding of a `date` field is `YYYY-MM-DD`, which is exactly the value\nformat `<input type=\"date\">` produces and consumes. So `task.due_date` can\nbe bound to the input's `value` with no parsing/formatting step in either\ndirection \u2014 same as every other field here, no new date library needed.\n\n## New elements\n\n1. **Due-date input** \u2014 `<input type=\"date\">`, styled as `.due-date-input`,\n   sibling to `.priority-select` in both `AddTask` and each `TaskRow`.\n2. **Clear control** \u2014 a small `\u00d7` button, shown only when a due date is\n   set, because `<input type=\"date\">`'s native clear affordance is\n   inconsistent across browsers (Firefox has none) and AC3 requires\n   clearing to always be possible.\n3. **Overdue badge** \u2014 `.overdue-badge`, a pill with an icon glyph *and* the\n   text \"Overdue\" (AC4: not colour alone).\n\n## AddTask (`frontend/src/components/AddTask.jsx`)\n\nAdd a due-date input between the priority select and the Add button.\nOptional \u2014 empty is a valid submission (AC1).\n\n```\n\u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n\u2502 [ What needs doing?      ] [Normal \u25be] [ \ud83d\udcc5 mm/dd/yyyy ] [Add] \u2502\n\u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n```\n\n- New state: `const [dueDate, setDueDate] = useState('')`.\n- `onAdd(trimmed, priority, dueDate || null)` \u2014 empty string becomes `null`,\n  never sent as `\"\"`.\n- Reset to `''` after submit, same lifecycle as `priority` resetting to\n  `'normal'`.\n- `aria-label=\"Due date (optional)\"` \u2014 the word \"optional\" in the label\n  itself, since this is the one field on the form that isn't required and\n  that should be discoverable without relying on a visual asterisk\n  convention this app doesn't otherwise use.\n- No clear button needed here \u2014 the field is empty by default and a user\n  who typed a date can just retype it; the clear-affordance problem only\n  matters for an *existing stored* value (row context, below).\n\n## TaskRow display state (`frontend/src/components/TaskList.jsx`)\n\nDue date sits immediately after the priority select, followed by the clear\nbutton (only when a value exists) and the overdue badge (only when\noverdue). This is a direct, un-modal edit exactly like priority \u2014 no\n\"Edit\" click required.\n\n**Populated, future due date, not overdue:**\n```\n\u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n\u2502 Buy groceries      [Normal \u25be] [\ud83d\udcc5 2026-08-20] [\u00d7]  [Edit][Done][Delete] \u2502\n\u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n```\n\n**Populated, overdue (past due, not done):**\n```\n\u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n\u2502 File taxes  [High \u25be] [\ud83d\udcc5 2026-08-01] [\u00d7]  [\u26a0 Overdue]  [Edit][Done][Delete] \u2502\n\u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n```\n\n**No due date set (default/empty state for this field):**\n```\n\u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n\u2502 Water plants        [Low \u25be] [\ud83d\udcc5 dd/mm/yyyy]  [Edit][Done][Delete] \u2502\n\u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n```\nNo clear button (nothing to clear) and no badge. The unset date input\nshows the browser's own placeholder \u2014 no custom \"No due date\" text needed,\nconsistent with the input being a live editable control, not a label.\n\n**Due date today (populated, not overdue \u2014 AC5):**\nSame layout as \"future due date, not overdue\" above \u2014 no visual distinction\nbetween \"due today\" and \"due in 10 days.\" The spec's AC5 only requires\n*absence* of the overdue marking, not a separate \"due today\" treatment,\nand adding one would be inventing a state the spec didn't ask for.\n\n**Overdue task marked done (AC7 \u2014 badge suppressed):**\n```\n\u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n\u2502 ~~Renew passport~~  [Normal \u25be] [\ud83d\udcc5 2026-07-15] [\u00d7]        [Delete]     \u2502\n\u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n```\nStrikethrough/dim via the existing `.task.done .task-title` rule \u2014 due\ndate input and clear button remain visible and editable (editing a done\ntask's due date is not restricted by the spec), badge is gone because\n`isOverdue()` is gated on `!task.done` (below).\n\n**Very long title + overdue badge together:** title uses the existing\n`.task-title { flex: 1 }`, which already absorbs long text without pushing\nfixed-width controls off-row; badge and date input keep their own\nintrinsic width via `white-space: nowrap`. Adding `flex-wrap: wrap` to\n`.task` (new, see CSS) lets the row wrap onto a second line on narrow\nviewports instead of overflowing, since this row now carries more controls\nthan the priority-only version did.\n\n## TaskRow editing state (title edit)\n\nUnchanged. Due date is edited independently of the title-edit mode, same\nas priority already is \u2014 `isEditing` only ever covered the title `<input>`\nand Save/Cancel, and stays that way.\n\n## Empty / Loading states\n\nNo change. Due date is a per-row field, not a filter or list mode \u2014 the\nspec's non-goals explicitly exclude sorting/filtering by due date or\noverdue status, so there is no \"no overdue tasks\" empty state and no\nloading-state difference to design.\n\n## Error state\n\nNo new error UI. A rejected due-date change (network failure, or the\nAC8 malformed-value case reachable only via direct API, not through this\ndate-picker) surfaces through the existing `run()` \u2192 `setError(e.message)`\n\u2192 `.error` banner path in `App.jsx`, identical to how a failed priority\nchange already surfaces. The native `<input type=\"date\">` itself prevents\nmalformed values from being typed through the UI at all, which is why AC8\nis scoped to direct API use only.\n\n## Overdue logic (drives the badge, implemented in `TaskList.jsx`)\n\n```js\nconst todayISO = () => new Date().toLocaleDateString('en-CA') // YYYY-MM-DD, local time\nconst isOverdue = (task) => !task.done && task.due_date != null && task.due_date < todayISO()\n```\nString comparison is valid because both sides are `YYYY-MM-DD` \u2014 lexical\norder matches chronological order for that format. `toLocaleDateString('en-CA')`\nis used (not `toISOString()`) specifically to get the *local* calendar\ndate, not UTC, so \"today\" matches what the user's own clock says \u2014 the\nspec's \"server's local date\" scoping is about the stored value, not this\ncomparison, which is a pure client-side same-day check against the\nbrowser's own clock.\n\n## Component/prop wiring\n\n- `TaskList` gains an `onDueDateChange` prop, threaded to `TaskRow`,\n  mirroring `onPriorityChange` exactly (`TaskList.jsx:15,32`).\n- `App.jsx` gains `onDueDateChange={(id, dueDate) => run(() => api.setDueDate(id, dueDate))}`,\n  passed to `TaskList`, mirroring `onPriorityChange` (`App.jsx:84`).\n- `AddTask`'s `onAdd` signature grows a third argument; its one caller in\n  `App.jsx:64` updates to `(title, priority, dueDate) => run(() => api.createTask(title, priority, dueDate))`.\n\n## Styling (`frontend/src/App.css`)\n\nNew rules, placed after the existing `.priority-select` block (the nearest\nprecedent):\n\n```css\n.task { flex-wrap: wrap; }\n\n.due-date-input {\n  padding: 0.4rem 0.6rem;\n  border: 1px solid #ccd2d6;\n  border-radius: 5px;\n  background: #fff;\n  color: #16191c;\n  font: inherit;\n  font-size: 0.85rem;\n}\n\n.due-date-clear {\n  padding: 0.4rem 0.6rem;\n  border: 1px solid #ccd2d6;\n  border-radius: 5px;\n  background: #fff;\n  color: #5a646c;\n  font-size: 0.85rem;\n  line-height: 1;\n  cursor: pointer;\n}\n.due-date-clear:hover { background: #f0f2f3; }\n\n.overdue-badge {\n  display: inline-flex;\n  align-items: center;\n  gap: 0.3rem;\n  padding: 0.2rem 0.55rem;\n  border-radius: 999px;\n  background: #fbe9e7;\n  color: #a3271d;\n  font-size: 0.8rem;\n  font-weight: 600;\n  white-space: nowrap;\n}\n```\n\n`.due-date-input` and `.due-date-clear` match `.priority-select`'s exact\npadding/border/font-size (`App.css:96-104`) so all three per-row controls\nread as one family at a glance \u2014 no new visual vocabulary introduced.\n\n`.overdue-badge` reuses the app's existing error palette\n(`.error { color: #a3271d; background: #fbe9e7 }`, `App.css:79`) rather\nthan inventing a new red, since \"overdue\" and \"error\" are the same\nsemantic register (something needs attention) and this app already has\nexactly one red in its palette.\n\n**Contrast, computed:**\n- `.overdue-badge` text `#a3271d` on its own background `#fbe9e7`:\n  **6.25:1** (needs 4.5:1 for text \u2014 passes).\n- `.overdue-badge` text `#a3271d` on the card background `#fff` (the badge\n  sits inline on the white `.task` card): **7.33:1** \u2014 passes either way.\n- `.due-date-clear` text `#5a646c` on `#fff`: **6.04:1** \u2014 passes.\n\n`#ccd2d6` borders on `.due-date-input`/`.due-date-clear` are the same\nborder colour already used on every input/button/select in this app\n(`App.css:14,18,98`); it measures ~1.53:1 against white, under the 3:1\nnon-text guideline, but that's a pre-existing app-wide convention, not a\nnew pairing introduced by this feature \u2014 out of scope to redesign here per\nthe non-goals (no other affected-area line touches existing controls'\nborders).\n\n## Accessibility\n\n- **Non-colour cue (AC4):** the badge's accessible name is the visible text\n  \"Overdue\" \u2014 the `\u26a0` glyph is `aria-hidden=\"true\"` and purely decorative,\n  so the requirement is met by text content, not by the icon or the colour.\n- **Labels:** every new/changed control has an explicit `aria-label`:\n  `\"Due date (optional)\"` (AddTask), `` `Due date for ${task.title}` ``\n  (row), `` `Clear due date for ${task.title}` `` (clear button) \u2014 same\n  pattern as the existing `` `Priority for ${task.title}` ``.\n- **Focus order:** DOM order is title \u2192 priority \u2192 due date \u2192 clear (if\n  present) \u2192 overdue badge (not focusable, it's `role=\"status\"`, not\n  interactive) \u2192 Edit \u2192 Done \u2192 Delete. Tab order follows visual left-to-\n  right order, consistent with the rest of the row.\n- **Target size:** `.due-date-clear` uses the same padding as\n  `.priority-select` (0.4rem 0.6rem) rather than a smaller icon-only\n  button, keeping it at the same touch target size as every other per-row\n  control \u2014 no new small-target element introduced.\n- **Live update:** the badge's `role=\"status\"` means a due-date edit that\n  causes a task to newly become (or stop being) overdue is announced to\n  screen reader users without requiring focus to move, matching the\n  existing `aria-live=\"polite\"` treatment already used for the empty-state\n  message (`TaskList.jsx:21`).\n\n## Acceptance criteria \u2192 design traceability\n\n| AC | Design element |\n|----|-----------------|\n| 1 | AddTask due-date input defaults to `''` \u2192 sent as `null`; nothing required to submit. |\n| 2 | AddTask due-date input value flows through `onAdd` \u2192 row displays it via `.due-date-input` bound to `task.due_date`. |\n| 3 | Row `.due-date-input` (`onChange`) sets/changes; `.due-date-clear` (shown only when set) clears to `null`. |\n| 4 | `.overdue-badge` \u2014 text \"Overdue\" + decorative icon, not colour-only; contrast computed above. |\n| 5 | `isOverdue()` uses `<` (strict), so a due date equal to today's local date renders the \"future/not overdue\" row layout. |\n| 6 | `isOverdue()` short-circuits `false` on `due_date == null`; future dates fail the `<` check. |\n| 7 | `isOverdue()` is gated on `!task.done` \u2014 done-task wireframe above shows the badge absent regardless of stored date. |\n| 8 | No UI path produces a malformed value \u2014 `<input type=\"date\">` constrains input; error, if any, surfaces via the existing `.error` banner. |\n| 9 | No new design surface \u2014 persistence is a backend/store concern, not a rendering one. |\n\n## Out of scope (per spec non-goals, not redesigned here)\n\n- No due-date column/sort, no due-date filter chip alongside\n  `TaskFilter`/`SearchTasks`.\n- No time-of-day picker \u2014 `type=\"date\"` only.\n- No \"due today\" distinct visual treatment (see AC5 wireframe note above).\n"}, "session_id": "120c4f69-2b5a-47aa-a596-94b78da02ca7"}}
