{"ts": "2026-08-17T12:43:53Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 76, "kind": "message", "text": "`docs/design.md` is written for Taiga #12.\n\n**Summary:**\n- Mirrors the priority control pattern throughout: `<input type=\"date\">` styled to match `.priority-select`, editable directly per-row, no edit-mode needed.\n- Adds a `.due-date-clear` button (shown only when a date is set) since native date-input clear support is inconsistent across browsers \u2014 needed to satisfy AC3's \"clearing must be possible.\"\n- Overdue badge (AC4) reuses the app's existing error red (`#a3271d` / `#fbe9e7`) rather than inventing a new colour, with the accessible cue being the visible text \"Overdue\" (icon is decorative/`aria-hidden`). Computed contrast: badge text-on-badge-bg 6.25:1, badge text-on-card 7.33:1, clear-button text 6.04:1 \u2014 all pass 4.5:1 for text.\n- Full wireframes for populated/overdue/done/unset states, plus explicit notes on why empty/loading/error states need no changes (non-goals exclude filtering/sorting by due date).\n- Exact prop wiring (`onDueDateChange` mirroring `onPriorityChange`) and file/line references for the developer stage.\n- Flagged one pre-existing gap (border contrast ~1.53:1, app-wide, not introduced by this feature) as explicitly out of scope rather than silently ignoring it.\n\nReady to hand off to the developer stage.", "meta": {"native_type": "assistant", "block_type": "text", "session_id": "120c4f69-2b5a-47aa-a596-94b78da02ca7"}}
